<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="037" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>My-requests list + feedback (email + in-app decision/response render) + thread-on-request (ConversationView on request)</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:031,036</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Client (Fluent v9) + BFF feedback/email + thread surface consuming the requester==caller reads (036) + 030 feedback/thread fields; touches shared external-access + Communication surfaces; tags frontend/bff-api — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Composition over established seams — my-requests render + reuse the /api/communications/send email path + mount ConversationView on the shared thread-on-request; no new architecture.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Consumes 036 (requester==caller reads) + 030 (feedback + thread fields); touches the shared external-access + Services/Communication BFF surfaces (conflict-check with teams-app-r1 + messaging/comm cluster); sequential.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031,036</deps>
    <tags>frontend, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Build the FR-24 feedback loop UI + delivery: (1) a my-requests list + detail rendering the caller's own requests (036 requester==caller reads) with legal's decision/response + downloadable response docs (030 feedback fields); (2) email-with-documents on legal review by reusing POST /api/communications/send with AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE (arbitrary recipient email + request association); (3) a thread-on-request — mount ConversationView on the request, reading the shared sprk_communicationthread lookup (030). FR-24 (feedback) + FR-27 (messaging) SHARE this one thread-on-request spine (§12 D). Reuse existing components; do NOT build a new list, email path, or thread model.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Fluent v9 + React 18 on @spaarke/ui-components (ConversationView, presets); app-only broker reads + the existing communications/send path (no OBO on the external plane, ADR-028/A3); ProblemDetails (ADR-019).</role>
  <goal>A workforce Front Door user sees a my-requests list (their own requests only, via 036) + a detail rendering legal's decision + response text + downloadable response docs (030 fields). On legal's MDA review, the requester is emailed via the existing POST /api/communications/send with AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE. A thread-on-request (ConversationView bound to the request's sprk_communicationthread, 030) renders on the request — the shared FR-24/FR-27 thread spine. User A never sees user B's feedback or thread (Tier-2 negative). Reuses ConversationView + communications/send + the shared thread; no new list/email/thread built.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-24 (spec.md line 255): a submitted request's decision + response documents flow back to the requester — (a) email-with-documents via the existing POST /api/communications/send (arbitrary recipient email + AttachmentDocumentIds resolved from SPE app-only + request association) triggered on legal's MDA review; (b) in-app — the my-requests detail renders legal's decision/response + downloadable response docs via the requester==caller endpoints (036). Additive schema (030): decision/outcome + response text + a response-document linkage distinct from the submitted-doc linkage. Live push/badge deferred (notification spine is systemuser-keyed; CIAM uses read-on-request). §12(D): FR-24 (feedback) + FR-27 (messaging) share ONE thread-on-request model — a request carries a conversation thread with the law department; the cross-boundary messaging spine (ConversationView + external thread endpoint) serves both. This task delivers the my-requests UI + feedback render + email trigger + the ConversationView on the shared thread (030 lookup); the external thread WRITE endpoint + ACS mint for cross-boundary posting is 052 (FR-27) — this task mounts the read/render on the shared spine.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md (FR-24 line 255; §12 D shared thread-on-request; FR-27 line 261 for the shared spine)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/036-submitter-authz-app-only-upload.poml (the requester==caller reads this UI renders)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/030-servicerequest-intake-schema.poml (decision/response feedback fields + the sprk_communicationthread lookup this task reads)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:2240 (POST /api/communications/send + AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE — the email-with-docs path to reuse)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/** ConversationView / ConversationWorkspace (mixed-principal chat, context-agnostic; mount on the request thread)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/** (the module-host shell + the 031 driver — mount my-requests + detail + the thread)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (binding BFF governance — Placement Justification + publish size); .claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>031 (Front Door group + module shell) + 036 (requester==caller reads + attribution) must be complete — the my-requests list/detail renders 036's scoped reads. 030 supplies the decision/response fields + the sprk_communicationthread lookup. 052 (FR-27) adds the external thread WRITE endpoint + ACS mint on the SAME shared thread spine (this task mounts the ConversationView read/render).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The my-requests list/detail MUST render the 036 requester==caller reads — the client never widens scope; user A sees only A's requests, decisions, response docs, and thread. Verify two-user isolation (Tier-2 negative).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Email-with-documents MUST reuse the existing POST /api/communications/send with AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE (CommunicationService.cs:2240) — do NOT build a new email path or a new attachment resolver. Trigger is on legal's MDA review.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The thread-on-request MUST mount ConversationView on the request's shared sprk_communicationthread lookup (030) — do NOT create a new thread entity or a second thread model. FR-24 + FR-27 share this one spine (§12 D); the external WRITE endpoint is 052.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">All external reads are app-only broker (no OBO); the caller token authenticates only to the BFF. No live SignalR push to the client (read-on-request per the amendment scope delta).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; zero hardcoded hex; verified light/dark/Teams theme + narrow Teams personal-tab width; all dialogs via @spaarke/ui-components presets (no hand-rolled Dialog, §11/ADR-050).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF addition (email trigger / feedback read): state the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); report dotnet publish size delta vs baseline 46.90 MB (ceiling ≤60 MB); run /conflict-check before the BFF PR — Services/Communication/** is a HEAVILY shared surface (email-r5, messaging-r1/r2/r3, notification-spine).</constraint>
  </constraints>
