    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Email-with-docs" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:2240">Reuse POST /api/communications/send + AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE; trigger on legal review.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Thread-on-request" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/** ConversationView">Mount ConversationView on the request's shared sprk_communicationthread (030) — the FR-24/FR-27 one-spine.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Scoped reads" location="projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/036-submitter-authz-app-only-upload.poml">Render only the 036 requester==caller reads; never widen scope client-side.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec.md FR-24 (line 255) + §12 D + FR-27 (line 261, for the shared spine) + ux-brief + 036/030 task files + CommunicationService.cs:2240 + ConversationView. Run /conflict-check for the external-access + Services/Communication BFF surfaces.</step>
    <step order="2">Client: build the my-requests list + detail in the Front Door module rendering the 036 requester==caller reads — status, legal's decision (030), response text, and downloadable response docs (distinct from the submitted doc). App-only reads; no scope widening.</step>
    <step order="3">Email trigger: on legal's MDA review, send the decision + response docs to the requester by reusing POST /api/communications/send with AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE + the request association. Do NOT build a new email path. (Wire the trigger BFF-side; keep the shared-surface footprint minimal.)</step>
    <step order="4">Thread-on-request: mount ConversationView on the request's shared sprk_communicationthread lookup (030) — render the read/history. The external WRITE (post) endpoint + ACS mint is 052; here render on the shared spine so FR-24 + FR-27 use one thread.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the required states (loading, empty, error, unentitled/denied, dark, Teams theme, keyboard, narrow width) per ux-brief §4 for the list, detail, and thread.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: client component tests for the my-requests list/detail (feedback render) + the ConversationView mount; two-user isolation (A never sees B's feedback/thread — Tier-2 negative). If a BFF email-trigger/read change exists, add KEEP-path integration tests (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;/DI/ctor tests, ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="7">Build: npm run build:prod (client); if BFF changed, dotnet publish -c Release + report size delta vs 46.90 MB + Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF (email trigger / feedback read)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/** — my-requests list + detail (feedback render) + ConversationView thread-on-request mounted on the shared sprk_communicationthread</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/** — email-with-docs trigger on legal review reusing POST /api/communications/send (AttachmentDocumentIds app-only) + the feedback read (if not already in 036)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/** — client component tests (feedback render + thread mount + two-user isolation negative); BFF KEEP-path tests if a BFF change exists</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a reviewed request, when the requester opens my-requests, then the detail renders legal's decision + response text + downloadable response docs (030 fields, distinct from the submitted doc).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given legal's MDA review, when it completes, then the requester is emailed via the existing POST /api/communications/send with the response docs attached (AttachmentDocumentIds resolved app-only from SPE) — no new email path in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a request, when its detail loads, then a ConversationView renders on the request's shared sprk_communicationthread (030) — the one FR-24/FR-27 thread spine (no second thread model).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (Tier-2 / two-user isolation): given user B's request + feedback + thread, when user A is signed in, then A never sees B's feedback or thread (client renders only 036's requester==caller reads).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the surfaces, when rendered in light/dark/Teams theme at narrow width, then semantic tokens adapt with zero hardcoded hex and no console errors.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Feedback render + thread">
      <steps><step>Open my-requests for a reviewed request</step><step>Verify decision/response + response docs; open the thread</step></steps>
      <expected>Decision/response + downloadable docs render; ConversationView shows the request thread; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Two-user isolation">
      <steps><step>Sign in as user A</step><step>Attempt to view user B's request/feedback/thread</step></steps>
      <expected>A sees only A's requests; B's feedback + thread never appear (Tier-2)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode; load inside a Teams-theme host at narrow width</step></steps>
      <expected>Zero hardcoded hex; tokens adapt across light/dark/Teams; readable at Teams personal-tab width</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Spec FR-24 (line 255) + §12(D) shared thread-on-request. Reuse POST /api/communications/send (email) + ConversationView (thread) + 036's requester==caller reads — no new list, email path, or thread model. Live push/badge deferred (read-on-request). The external thread WRITE endpoint + ACS mint (cross-boundary posting) is 052 (FR-27) — this task mounts the read/render on the shared spine. Services/Communication is heavily shared → /conflict-check mandatory before the BFF PR. Use build:prod per CLAUDE.md §12 / AP-1.</notes>
